ith kernel = block size; mean-pool is the natural weaker comparison.</item>\\n<item>A3. Selection is query-conditioned top-k over unit vectors, applied per generated token (or per query block) using dot-product similarity.</item>\\n<item>A4. Dynamic lookup is the load-bearing novelty to isolate; static-pool / recency-k / random-k are the right internal controls.</item>\\n<item>A5. A 7B-class open backbone with a 2k-4k base window (Llama-2-7B / Mistral-7B family) is acceptable for the ablation.</item>\\n<item>A6. The interesting exploitation range starts around 8k and goes up; effects of memory lookup on short contexts are likely degenerate.</item>\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1. Backbone choice and base context length.</item>\\n<item>U2. Availability of a reference InfLLM implementation to ablate, vs. need to rebuild from the paper.</item>\\n<item>U3. Compute envelope (GPU-hours, model scale) - drives whether F4 budget sweep and length sweep survive.</item>\\n<item>U4. Evaluation suite: LongBench / InfiniteBench / L-Eval / custom mix, and whether same suite across all cells.</item>\\n<item>U5. Default block size and k for the F1=InfLLM-dynamic reference cell.</item>\\n<item>U6. Whether positional-encoding handling for memory units is in-scope as a factor or must be frozen.</item>\\n<item>U7. Whether the design is hard-fixed to training-free, or whether a fine-tune-the-conv auxiliary cell is wanted.</item>\\n<item>U8. Scope of \\\"unit representation\\\": first-token / attention-pooled variants in or out.</item>\"]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-321103ff-335a-42db-9ba0-956821d6aa16", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "kind": "ActionEvent", "source_event_index": 12}
